**The finding the county should hear: the RESKIN audit note on this contract is stale.** The E4 layer composes headless now — the first idle view publishes a full `now.motor` at `viewVersion: 2`, and the secure is gated on `objective.arrived` at `HeadlessContractSim.ts:1210`. The tow is a real two-leg fuel/distance problem: 36.7wu to the hulk, `stop` then *moves* to the corridor's gate end for another 31.6wu, 22.8 fuel needed against 36 in the whole run, with a storm clock that makes the same distance cost 33% more. I harvested all three tar nodes rather than the two the arithmetic needs, precisely because a storm on either leg would have stranded a two-node tank. The audit predates `48ef7df8d`.

The honest qualifier is in the report: the errand ended at t=42.8s and waves 3–12 were ordinary stationary survival. Half a reskin, not a whole one. `GRADE` also proved nearly worthless here — only 4.4 of 68.4 wu travelled rode graded ground, because the Hauler drives straight lines and this errand routes around its own road.

Two of my own prior lessons carried it, and one of them had to be **inverted**: gen-9's "chain different seam ids" is correct near seams and fatal at 50wu — tune 1 banked one 5-gold pan per wave and died at wave 5; stacking six orders on the *same* id was worth 4× and secured. Gen-12's suffix-sum build gating finally got proven: one trip home buys the whole batch instead of one turret per 100wu round trip.

Margin: wide on the errand (13.2 of 36 fuel unspent, never near dry), thin on the fort (hero bottomed at 39.6/150 in wave 6, held 55/175 with threats pinned at the 60 ceiling, on three turrets and eight palisades).

Report sections 1–4 are in `gauntlet-report.md` ready to copy verbatim; `gauntlet-outcome.json` was current after every run. No tracked files touched — `git status` shows only the untracked `artifacts/heat11/`.
